					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2203795&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608475972" alt="Kalinin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2203795)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;" >Kalinin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1440117239 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Aug 2015 00:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2361501">
									

<p>To take somewhat of a political stance with my voting, I am neutral voting with the hopes of changing that to an upvote if this is polished a bit. Ordinarily, I will downvote on the basis of flawed execution (which is flawed writing), but this article is <em>exactly</em> the kind of thing I want to see on the site when it comes to the portrayal of art. It's odd, but there are enough threads going throughout it that it doesn't come across as weird for the sake of weird.</p>
<p>There are some problems that prevent me from enjoying it as much as I could be, however:</p>
<ul>
<li>The addendum doesn't need to be collapsed, IMO. The article is short enough that I think you can just have it there without running afoul of the Wall of Text contingent<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-858337-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-858337-1')">1</a></sup>.</li>
<li>Why is the title of the book redacted? Am I missing something?</li>
<li>The second paragraph of the description could use tightening. I would couch the description of the book's literary style a bit; I'm all for the Foundation having literary experts on hand, I really am, but the description of it being an amalgam of these specific styles is a little too cut-and-dry. I also think you need to clarify the &quot;30 minutes of inactivity&quot; part. I had to read it a couple of times to figure out that that meant 30 minutes of not being read by someone.</li>
<li>&quot;Researchers have no reason to presume the theoretical limit of SCP-2811 is not infinite.&quot; This sentence is a little clunky. I think you could get away with &quot;There is no theoretical limit to the amount of text that SCP-2811 may contain&quot; or something.</li>
<li>Clarify the part about how the additions affect the overall narrative; I'm not <em>quite</em> sure what exactly you're getting at.</li>
<li>Not sure why the blackboxes in the addendum are necessary.</li>
</ul>
<p>I dislike the act of holding votes hostage to personal preference, but I think that the concerns I've outlined above are probably shared by enough people that it would likely improve the article for people other than me. With some work, I will enthusiastically support this article. The concept is intriguing to me.</p>
